# A Windows checkout must behave like the Linux CI runner.
#
# Without this, git's core.autocrlf setting hands a Windows contributor CRLF files,
# and Prettier (which expects LF by default) then reports every file as unformatted.
# A fresh-clone dry run found exactly that: 238 files failing on Windows, none on
# Linux. Normalising on commit and checkout makes `npm run prettier:verify` mean the
# same thing on both.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary or opaque assets: never convert these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.resource binary
